17] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428935 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428936 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428937 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428938 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428939 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428940 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428941 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428942 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1031 "Introduction to Integration by Parts" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1033 317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1034 1.4476087343369344 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050929 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7280f087-059d-5524-8f8b-a1fe79b4ef9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163432 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163432 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163432 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163432 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163432 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186163437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163432 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163432 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163432 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "093657e8-681a-5676-ae66-c18d57c5ed27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163433 #edb/ref 1080 "2 - 3z^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163433 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163433 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9cf0dac3-4d13-5a2d-aa90-8c808e699149" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163434 #edb/ref 1080 "z^{2} + 3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163434 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163434 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d1ae1205-4a7e-5718-9583-f6be0276a73a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163435 #edb/ref 1080 "2 - z^{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163435 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163435 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b9e4fac-b2f0-5352-84e4-be868e42015a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163436 #edb/ref 1080 "3 - z^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163436 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163436 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "71029930-18eb-5cde-99b5-81a391550102" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163437 #edb/ref 1080 "1 - 2z^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163437 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163437 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "75f39f26-5b0b-5df6-9d3c-cb5d05529e0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166701 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9035" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166701 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\ln(x + y).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z= x + y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form $z'(x) = f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166701 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "870077e3-99f9-52b9-ac39-26bbc3827466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166701 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x + y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = 1 + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form $z'(x) = f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = \\ln z+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z) = \\ln z + 1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166702 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9037" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166702 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = x + y.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y) = x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166702 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3145755-b414-57e5-8039-04ceb1a3a5f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166702 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz = x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = 1 + \\,\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x} - 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form $z'(x) = f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}z}{\\textrm{d}x}  = z+1.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{z+1}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{z+1}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|z+1| & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\ln{|x+y+1|}  = x + C\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y) = \\ln{|x+y+1|}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166851 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166851 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166851 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166851 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186244167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166851 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186244168 #edb/ref 17592186045