7] [17592186243735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243735 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186243378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243735 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243735 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243735 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186242285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243735 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a1be1d49-45f2-5b7f-a18f-ad5c635c720b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186241935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186241955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243872 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243872 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243872 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243872 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186242529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243872 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f8b85e2a-be80-5ab9-ba75-e0dd0adbbf66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244169 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244169 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108802" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244169 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244169 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={tan}^{2}⁡(3x-5y).\n$$\n\nUsing a substitution of the form $z=3x-5y,$ transform the differential equation into an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z).$ What is the function $f(z)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244169 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e81268a9-ddfd-5f92-b961-b0aa841e7817" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244169 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=3x-5y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3-5\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={tan}^{2}⁡z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=3-5{tan}^{2}⁡z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=3-5{tan}^{2}⁡z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244177 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244177 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108841" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244177 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244177 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{x+y}-x-y}{x+y}.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=C-x,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244177 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1afbf5f-1cd8-5fe7-a308-11eeef08401b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244177 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=x+y.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=1+\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-1 & =\\frac{{e}^{z}-z}{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{e}^{z}}{z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{z}{{e}^{z}}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int z{e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing integration by parts on the left side,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=z & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-z} & \\,⟹\\,v=-{e}^{-z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int z{e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -z{e}^{-z}+\\int {e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -z{e}^{-z}-{e}^{-z} & =x+C \\\\ -{e}^{-z}(z+1) & =x+K \\\\ {e}^{-z}(z+1) & =C-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-K.$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n{e}^{-x-y}(x+y+1)=C-x\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)={e}^{-x-y}(x+y+1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272464 #edb/ref 1080 "3{e}^{3x-y}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272464 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272464 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08c6a07b-8faf-5324-b53c-a2c58ed30c92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272649 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{y-3x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272649 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272649 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d7cc5e8-497a-5d6f-aec1-4ad07e072b25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272742 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{3x-y}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272742 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272742 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28394a0c-f284-5ba2-9531-bf15a477e453" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273815 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{y-3x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273815 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186273815 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a53691e1-9247-57ee-a1ef-92baf61ae110" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274492 #edb/ref 1080 "-{e}^{3x-y}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274492 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186274492 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ede43097-d715-52fa-8f73-02118dc5234a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186272742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186273815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186274492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275010 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275010 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275010 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186272742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275010 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d44bbdb7-74e5-579b-a1f0-5dcb97d86e01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275238 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186275010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275238 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275238 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275238 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3-{e}^{y-3x}.\n$$\n\n \nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ng(x,y)=x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275238 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2be2a98-4693-5e20-8a16-811d290d52b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275238 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz=y-3x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+3 & =3-{e}^{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing this equation in the form ${z}^{′}(x)=f(z)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{z}.\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is separable. So, we separate the variables and integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{-z}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ -\\int {e}^{-z}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{-z} & =x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the equation in terms of $y$ and $x$ using our original substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n{e}^{3x-y}=x+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x,y)={e}^{3x-y}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
